    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Sensitivity B — No phylogenetic random effect\"\n---\n\n\n\n## What this tests\n\nThe primary models place a phylogenetic random effect\n`(1 | gr(sp_ncbi, cov = A))` on every species-level intercept, using a\ncorrelation matrix `A` derived from an Open Tree of Life scaffold. That scaffold\nis a pragmatic comparative tree, not a fully resolved, time-calibrated phylogeny\n(protocol §3.6): its topology is assembled from multiple sources, unresolved\nnodes are resolved algorithmically, and branch lengths are assigned by Grafen's\nmethod. This analysis refits each included moderator model with the phylogenetic\nterm **removed**, keeping the `ref_id` study effect and everything else fixed, to\ncheck that conclusions do not depend strongly on that scaffold. The full dataset\nis used (no sample-size restriction).\n\n## How it was fit\n\nFit on `totoro`, not at render — 4 chains × 4,000 iterations (2,000 warmup),\n`adapt_delta = 0.97`, `max_treedepth = 15`, `cmdstanr`.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nformula <- build_ls_formula(moderator, has_phylogeny = FALSE)   # drop (1 | gr(sp_ncbi, cov = A))\nV       <- diag(dat_mod$vi_lnM_safe)\nfit     <- fit_ls_model(\n  dat_mod, formula,\n  build_ls_priors(formula, dat_mod, V, A = NULL),\n  V = V, A = NULL, mcmc_args = default_mcmc_args)\n```\n:::\n\n\n## Convergence diagnostics\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table table-striped table-condensed\" style=\"width: auto !important; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n<caption>Convergence diagnostics (4 chains, 2000 post-warmup draws each).</caption>\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Moderator </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Max R̂ </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Min bulk ESS </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Min tail ESS </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Divergences </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Max-treedepth hits </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Comparison design (m02) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0090 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 619 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 988 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Disturbance context (m01) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0044 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 903 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1779 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Environmental-change context (m08) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0094 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 481 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1029 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Phenotypic vs genetic study (m07) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0084 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 438 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1216 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Elapsed time — log₁₀ generations (m04) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0094 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 548 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1094 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Elapsed time — log₁₀ years (m03) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0073 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 460 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1095 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Trait type (m05) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0052 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 538 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1183 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n`````\n:::\n:::\n\n\nAll models converged cleanly (R̂ < 1.01, no divergent transitions) — unsurprising,\nsince dropping the dense phylogenetic covariance removes the hardest part of the\nposterior geometry.\n\n## Reading the tables\n\nRaw location–scale coefficients on treatment coding: the **Intercept** row is the\nreference-level value, each other row the difference from it. The matched\n**primary** (phylogeny-included) coefficient is shown alongside, and the\n**Stability** column reads *consistent* when the two share sign and the same 95%\ncredible-interval conclusion, **DIFFERS** (highlighted) otherwise.\n\n**Overall:**  3 of 36 moderator coefficients change their credible-interval conclusion relative to the primary fit. \n\n## Results by moderator\n\n\n### Disturbance context (m01)\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table table-striped table-condensed\" style=\"width: auto !important; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n<caption>Disturbance context (m01)</caption>\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Sub-model </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Term </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Sensitivity β [95% CrI] </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Primary β [95% CrI] </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Stability </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;vertical-align: top !important;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(255, 243, 205, 255) !important;\" rowspan=\"7\"> Location (mean lnM) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(255, 243, 205, 255) !important;\"> Intercept (ref.) </td>\n   <td style=